{"annotations":{"destructiveHint":false,"idempotentHint":true,"openWorldHint":false,"readOnlyHint":true,"title":"Compare selling Bitcoin with borrowing against it"},"description":"Illustrates the liquidity from selling an amount of Bitcoin after tax, against borrowing on it as collateral, and what each leaves at a later price. Deterministic; the same model as the live Borrowing Against Bitcoin explorer, in USD. mode btc_to_btc borrows BTC at ltvPct (default 95%); the lender keeps a 5% fee from the collateral, so the rest is retained; fiat_loan borrows USD at ltvPct (default 50%) with simple interest (default 8% a year for 1 year), and returns a liquidation price where the loan reaches 80% of the collateral's value. Tax is a flat rate on the whole sale value, from taxRatePct or the region's default (us 20%, au 45%, illustrative only). horizon sets the later price as a multiple of spot: flat (x1), up50 (x1.5), up100 (x2), stress30 (x0.7), stress50 (x0.5); never a forecast. Stress rows at 30% and 50% below spot are always included. A negative or non-finite termYears is rejected. Other out-of-range values are clamped as the page clamps them, and the result echoes what was used. btcPrice is a spot price in USD supplied by the caller (btcPriceUsd is accepted as an alias). Without it the server's cached USD market reference is used, labelled live, or a fixed illustrative price of 100000 USD when that reference is unavailable. The illustrative price is not a market quotation. It names no lender, does not assess suitability or eligibility, and recommends neither path.","inputSchema":{"$schema":"https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema","additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"btcAmount":{"type":"number"},"btcPrice":{"exclusiveMinimum":0,"type":"number"},"btcPriceUsd":{"deprecated":true,"description":"Alias of btcPrice, in USD.","exclusiveMinimum":0,"type":"number"},"horizon":{"enum":["flat","up50","up100","stress30","stress50"],"type":"string"},"interestRatePct":{"typ